.godot/
.DS_Store

## Deliberately NOT ignored: *.uid
##
## Godot 4.4+ writes a .uid file next to every script and imported resource,
## and its identity system depends on them being version-controlled -- they are
## what keeps references intact across a rename or a move. Ignoring them looks
## tempting the first time a pull collides on one, but the collision means the
## opposite: somebody added a script without a .uid, the editor generated one
## locally, and the two met when it was finally committed.
##
## The fix is `godot --headless --path . --import` and committing the result,
## which `_test_every_script_has_a_uid` in tests/test_runner.gd now enforces.

# Generated by tools/collect_review_bundle.sh -- probe output, screen renders
# and the packed archive. Regenerable from the script, so the script is the
# artefact worth versioning and this is not.
review_bundle/
review_bundle.zip

# Render galleries written by the tools/render_*.gd probes. Seventeen megabytes
# of PNG on this branch alone, and every frame of it is one command away:
# `xvfb-run -a godot --path . --rendering-method gl_compatibility --script
# tools/render_all_kits.gd`. Same rule as review_bundle/ above -- the tool is
# the artefact worth versioning, not its output. Note the renderers must NOT be
# run with --headless: the gallery hangs and writes zero images.
#
# artifacts/title_desk_draft/ stays tracked, because it is a design decision
# somebody argued about rather than a probe's latest output.
artifacts/all-colourways/
artifacts/all-kits/
artifacts/cani-ear-ab/
artifacts/feature-axes/
artifacts/headshot-previews/
artifacts/identity-budget/
artifacts/mark-previews/
artifacts/simi-colourways/
artifacts/squad-after/
artifacts/squad-identity/
artifacts/style-drafts/
artifacts/world-geography/

# Python bytecode from the tools/ scripts. One .pyc reached the tree before this
# rule existed; it is a build product of a file already versioned beside it.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
